  "final_text": "I refused this run rather than generating an input file. Here's why:\n\nThe requested kinematics are physically impossible with a 2.2 GeV beam. For `ep \u2192 e'p\u03b7` at W = 2.0 GeV, Q\u00b2 = 3.0 GeV\u00b2, the required energy transfer is \u03bd = (W\u00b2 \u2212 M_p\u00b2 + Q\u00b2)/(2M_p) \u2248 3.26 GeV (using M_p = 0.938272 GeV, the value hard-coded in `eta/exclurad.F`). Since \u03bd = E \u2212 E\u2032 and E\u2032 \u2265 0, the beam energy alone must exceed 3.26 GeV \u2014 and once you fold in the scattering-angle constraint (Q\u00b2 \u2264 4EE\u2032, maximized at \u03b8 = 180\u00b0), the true minimum beam energy is about **3.48 GeV**. A 2.2 GeV beam can't reach this point at any angle (it implies a negative scattered-electron energy).\n\nTo proceed, you'd need to either:\n- raise the beam energy (e.g. to the CLAS12 default 6.53 GeV already used in `eta/input.dat`), or\n- pick a Q\u00b2 reachable at 2.2 GeV for W = 2.0 GeV (roughly Q\u00b2 \u2272 0.3 GeV\u00b2 depending on angle).\n\nDetails are recorded in `outcome.json`; no input file was written since generating one would just feed EXCLURAD an unreachable kinematic point."
